// Title: Remote Access Tool - ScreenConnect Execution
// Sigma ID: 57bff678-25d1-4d6c-8211-8ca106d12053
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-02-13 | Modified: 2023-03-05
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: An adversary may use legitimate desktop support and remote access software, such as Team Viewer,
//   Go2Assist, LogMein, AmmyyAdmin, etc, to establish an interactive command and control channel to
//   target systems within networks. These services are commonly used as legitimate technical support
//   software, and may be allowed by application control within a target environment. Remote access
//   tools like VNC, Ammyy, and Teamviewer are used frequently when compared with other legitimate
//   software commonly used by adversaries. (Citation: Symantec Living off the Land)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the tool
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1219/T1219.md#atomic-test-5---screenconnect-application-download-and-install-on-windows
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_screenconnect.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "ScreenConnect Service" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName =~ "ScreenConnect" or ProcessVersionInfoCompanyName =~ "ScreenConnect Software"
